{#
  ContextualHelp macro — a help button that opens a popover with
  explanatory content.

  HTML tag: <div>
  CSS class: contextual-help

  The Nunjucks macro does not generate ids dynamically. The
  consumer can pass `params.id` for the panel; the trigger uses
  this value as `aria-controls`. When `params.id` is omitted the
  panel id falls back to "contextual-help-panel".

  No script: the panel is popover="auto" and the trigger names it with
  command="toggle-popover" commandfor (Chrome 135, Firefox 144, Safari
  26.2) and popovertarget (Chrome 114, Firefox 125, Safari 17), so the
  browser opens it, and closes it on Escape and on a click outside it
  (light dismiss).

  Accessibility:
    - The trigger is <button> with aria-haspopup="dialog", aria-controls
      and an aria-label (its accessible name).
    - Closed, the trigger carries no static aria-expanded: nothing would
      update it without script, and the browser exposes the expanded state
      of a popovertarget trigger itself.
    - The panel uses role="dialog", named by `label` as the trigger is.

  Params:
    label         string   REQUIRED. aria-label for the help trigger.
    triggerLabel  string   REQUIRED. Visible (escaped) text of the trigger,
                           such as "?" or "؟". No default: the glyph is the
                           consumer's, per script and locale.
    triggerHtml   string   Raw HTML for the trigger content instead (an
                           icon); wins over triggerLabel.
    triggerText   string   Older name for triggerLabel, still accepted.
    expanded      boolean  Default false. true renders the panel shown in
                           place, without the popover attribute (a popover
                           cannot start open without script), and the
                           trigger with aria-expanded="true".
    id           string   Optional id for the panel.
    text         string   Plain text content (escaped) for the panel.
    html         string   Raw HTML content for the panel.
    classes      string
    attributes   object

  Usage:
    {% from "components/contextual-help/macro.njk" import contextualHelp %}
    {{ contextualHelp({
      id: "field-help",
      label: "Help",
      triggerLabel: "?",
      html: "<p>Type your full legal name.</p>"
    }) }}
#}
{%- macro contextualHelp(params) -%}
{%- set p = params | default({}) -%}
{%- set panelId = p.id | default('contextual-help-panel') -%}
<div
  class="contextual-help{% if p.classes %} {{ p.classes }}{% endif %}"
  {%- if p.attributes %}{% for k, v in p.attributes %} {{ k }}="{{ v }}"{% endfor %}{% endif %}
>
  <button
    class="contextual-help-trigger"
    type="button"
    aria-label="{{ p.label }}"
    aria-haspopup="dialog"
    aria-controls="{{ panelId }}"
    {%- if p.expanded %} aria-expanded="true"
    {%- else %} command="toggle-popover" commandfor="{{ panelId }}" popovertarget="{{ panelId }}"{% endif %}
  >
    {%- if p.triggerHtml -%}{{ p.triggerHtml | safe }}
    {%- elif p.triggerLabel -%}{{ p.triggerLabel }}
    {%- elif p.triggerText -%}{{ p.triggerText }}
    {%- endif -%}
  </button>
  <div
    class="contextual-help-panel"
    id="{{ panelId }}"
    role="dialog"
    {%- if p.label %} aria-label="{{ p.label }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if not p.expanded %} popover="auto"{% endif %}
  >
    {%- if p.html -%}{{ p.html | safe }}
    {%- elif p.text -%}{{ p.text }}
    {%- elif caller -%}{{ caller() }}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>
{%- endmacro -%}
